omi-dom-orch
00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Fourteenth omi-dom module: contrasting-orchestrator, with the spatial-gnn and edge-ngram pieces it runs on, as src/zorch.c (orch.rc). Every target on six graphs (cycles of 2, 4 and 5, complete graphs of 4 and 5, a path of 4; features 1<<v) converges as the module does, 116 runs. Its four assertions pass; two are type checks, and the other two ask only for the target it has just computed. Finding: the digest is linear, and one epoch moves it by exactly the XOR of the admitted neighbours of odd degree (checked for every filter over four epochs on each graph), since a neighbour's feature enters once per edge. So on a graph whose degrees are all even (every cycle, the module's own 4-cycle among them, and the complete graph of 5) no filter and no epoch moves the digest: it is the XOR of the features, and converge reaches diff 0 for that one target only (1 of 4, 16, 32), never by entraining the filter. Only odd degrees let it move: complete4 converges for 4 targets, path4 for 2. A filter here is the set of node indices it admits, the module's chained closures as masks ANDed.

